---
permalink: /cocktails/search.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  WHAT THE "SEARCH FOR ANYTHING" BOX SEARCHES ON A DRINK PAGE -- GitHub issue
  #1050, 2026-09-15. The drinks' half of food/search.json; read that file's
  comment for the shape and the reasoning, which are the same. Fetched by
  assets/js/page-search.js from the box _includes/back-to-index.html renders.

  THE SAME LIST THE INDEX SHOWS. `all_drinks` is assembled exactly as
  cocktails/index.html assembles it -- the gated public collection, plus the
  drafts ONLY under `site.show_drafts`, which _config_local.yml declares and
  production does not (#235). tests/test_rendered_pages.py holds the two lists
  equal in a production build.

  WHAT A DRINK CARRIES HERE. `moods` is the drink's mood list, which the MOOD
  and HASSLE groups both count (one filter with two headings, MANUAL 9.13 --
  the split is taxonomy.yml's `mood_groups`). `ing` is the CARD'S ingredient
  line, label for label, from _plugins/cocktail_card_ingredients.rb: the card
  name is the chip the index's HAS TO HAVE field offers (MANUAL 9.10.1, "cards
  and search read the VOCABULARY"), so a word chosen here is a word the index
  can apply.

  A JOINED "X OR Y" LABEL IS NEVER OFFERED -- #1051. `card_ingredients` marks
  one of these with `generics: 2` (or more): the card still prints
  "aged rum or Jamaican rum" as a true fact about the pour, but that string
  names no single HAS TO HAVE chip, so omnisearch would offer a result that
  matches nothing when clicked (the `?ing=` grammar matches a chip WHOLE,
  MANUAL 13.13). Excluded here rather than filtered in page-search.js, so the
  dropdown never has to know the difference between a real ingredient and a
  joined one -- the feed simply never contains it.

  IT FAILS OPEN: only a row that SAYS it joins two or more generics is left
  out. The first version kept `where: "generics", 1`, which also dropped a
  row with no generic at all (`generics: 0`, labelled from its item) and
  EVERY row on a `jekyll serve` started before the plugin gained the field
  (MANUAL §1: plugins are not reloaded). Helen, testing it on 2026-09-15:
  "Now the only things it returns are cocktail names. Please put it back."
  A missing `generics` is nil, and nil compares false against 1 in Liquid,
  so such a row is kept.

  `items_label` IS PLACEHOLDER COPY, Helen's to write (MANUAL 13.12).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign this_site = site.data.sites[page.site_key] -%}
{%- assign groups = site.data.cocktails.taxonomy.mood_groups -%}
{%- assign all_drinks = site.cocktail_recipes -%}
{%- if site.show_drafts -%}
  {%- assign all_drinks = all_drinks | concat: site.cocktail_drafts -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sorted_drinks = all_drinks | sort: "title" -%}
{
  "site": {{ page.site_key | jsonify }},
  "home": {{ this_site.home | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "items_label": "drinks",
  "groups": [
    {"kind": "mood", "label": "Mood", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.mood | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "hassle", "label": "Hassle", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.hassle | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "ingredient", "label": "Has to have", "param": "ing", "field": "ing"}
  ],
  "items": [
    {%- for d in sorted_drinks %}
    {% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{"t": {{ d.title | jsonify }}, "u": {{ d.url | relative_url | jsonify }}, "moods": {{ d.mood | jsonify }}, "ing": [{%- assign _first_ing = true -%}{%- for ing in d.card_ingredients -%}{%- unless ing.generics > 1 -%}{%- unless _first_ing %}, {% endunless -%}{{ ing.label | jsonify }}{%- assign _first_ing = false -%}{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}]}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
